<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>The economic issues and policy in France - RFI</title><description>Follow any political information, cultural, sporting and live streaming on RFI. The latest information, news and events in France, Europe and around the world.</description><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/</link><lastBuildDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 10:46:35 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>France</category><title>French PM visits Mayotte to speed up 'slow' reconstruction after cyclone</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260826-french-pm-visits-mayotte-to-speed-up-slow-reconstruction-after-cyclone</link><description>
Prime Minister Sébastien Lecornu arrives in the French overseas territory of Mayotte on Wednesday to try to speed up the reconstruction of the archipelago, 18 months after Cyclone Chido caused widespread destruction.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/adc78510-5d78-11f0-9d19-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-64FJ6ZQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/adc78510-5d78-11f0-9d19-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-64FJ6ZQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9efd8954-a12d-11f1-9d4b-c95053c4254a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 10:46:09 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/adc78510-5d78-11f0-9d19-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-64FJ6ZQ.jpg">© PATRICK MEINHARDT / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Looking up: French radio enthusiast captures ISS signals from his garage</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260825-looking-up-french-radio-enthusiast-captures-iss-signals-from-his-garage</link><description>
Astronaut Sophie Adenot made history this month as the first French woman to perform a spacewalk. Back on Earth, space enthusiasts across France are finding their own ways to reach for the stars. In the second episode of a five-part series, RFI hears from Vincent Plousey, a radio ham from Tavaux in eastern France whose hobby is picking up signals from the ISS using homemade antennas built in his garage.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/47b9e1ae-9fc2-11f1-8cd5-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/DSC-0284.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/47b9e1ae-9fc2-11f1-8cd5-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/DSC-0284.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8dd209ca-9fc0-11f1-b750-e347e9354ddc</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 13:48:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/47b9e1ae-9fc2-11f1-8cd5-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/DSC-0284.jpg">© Baptiste Coulon / RFI</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French village reels from tornado that damaged hundreds of homes</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260825-french-village-reels-from-tornado-that-damaged-hundreds-of-homes</link><description>
Hundreds of damaged homes, widespread power cuts and blocked roads confronted residents of southwestern France on Tuesday after a tornado tore through the village of Pomas, injuring 39 people, two of them critically.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4d47dd7a-a052-11f1-9f0c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6F74ZQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4d47dd7a-a052-11f1-9f0c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6F74ZQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4d36d51c-a04c-11f1-93b2-dd9b3ccbcf49</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 09:59:30 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4d47dd7a-a052-11f1-9f0c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6F74ZQ.jpg">AFP - CYRILLE KALDOR / UGC / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France's Sophie Adenot returns to the void for second spacewalk in a week</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260825-french-astronaut-sophie-adenot-to-make-second-spacewalk-to-finish-repairs</link><description>
French astronaut Sophie Adenot on Tuesday stepped outside the International Space Station (ISS) for the second time, a week after she became the first French woman to perform a spacewalk. Adenot and US astronaut Anil Menon are due to finish replacing a faulty antenna on the ISS after running out of time during their first spacewalk on 18 August.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c386df8a-9fc2-11f1-b73a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-18T193750Z-1637559858-RC211NAFX3V1-RTRMADP-3-SPACE-SPACEWALK.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c386df8a-9fc2-11f1-b73a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-18T193750Z-1637559858-RC211NAFX3V1-RTRMADP-3-SPACE-SPACEWALK.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d50039fa-9fc2-11f1-b33b-e347e9354ddc</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 05:57:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c386df8a-9fc2-11f1-b73a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-18T193750Z-1637559858-RC211NAFX3V1-RTRMADP-3-SPACE-SPACEWALK.jpg">via REUTERS - NASA</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Centre-left Glucksmann enters French presidential race as left tries to unite</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260824-centre-left-glucksmann-enters-french-presidential-race-as-left-tries-to-unite</link><description>
French centre-left politician Raphael Glucksmann has announced his candidacy for next year's presidential election, seeking to challenge hard-left leader Jean-Luc Melenchon to lead France's fractured left, as a campaign increasingly dominated by the far right takes shape.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f403b9ee-9f22-11f1-8810-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6C88EV.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f403b9ee-9f22-11f1-8810-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6C88EV.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4365a168-9f83-11f1-8a80-dd78f7da95c3</guid><pubDate>Mon, 24 Aug 2026 06:18:46 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f403b9ee-9f22-11f1-8810-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6C88EV.jpg">© Julie Sebadelha/AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Scorching summer takes toll on bees and honey harvests in France</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260823-scorching-summer-takes-toll-on-bees-and-honey-harvests-in-france</link><description>
France produces 20,000 tonnes of honey each year, but successive heatwaves and persistent drought across Europe this summer are impacting bee populations as flowering plants dry out and colonies struggle to find food. Beekeeper Romain Lacotte and his family farm 1,000 hives in Haute-Corrèze, central France, an area considered one of the country's natural water towers. But even there, he tells RFI, high temperatures and lack of rain are taking their toll.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/096fa74a-9ae9-11f1-9b51-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP080311039012.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/096fa74a-9ae9-11f1-9b51-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP080311039012.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">11563ee0-9ae1-11f1-bfbb-0f799d11d84e</guid><pubDate>Sun, 23 Aug 2026 15:44:53 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/096fa74a-9ae9-11f1-9b51-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP080311039012.jpg">© ASSOCIATED PRESS - Jacquelyn Martin </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Saudi crown prince heads to France as Paris seeks closer Gulf ties</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260823-saudi-crown-prince-heads-to-france-as-paris-seeks-closer-gulf-ties</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron will host Saudi Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman on Sunday for a two-day official visit, as Paris looks to deepen ties with Riyadh against a backdrop of war in the Middle East.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e54fd332-0eb7-11ee-9ed7-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23167416134566.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e54fd332-0eb7-11ee-9ed7-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23167416134566.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">128f22b8-9d66-11f1-be58-479c257d485f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 23 Aug 2026 07:05:25 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e54fd332-0eb7-11ee-9ed7-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23167416134566.jpg">© AP - Michel Euler </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Eroding coastlines unearth and destroy slave graves in French Caribbean</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260822-eroding-coastlines-unearth-and-destroy-slave-graves-in-french-caribbean</link><description>
Rising seas and coastal erosion are exposing the graves of enslaved people on beaches in the French Caribbean departments of Martinique and Guadeloupe, bringing long-buried remains back into view. Archaeologists say the retreating coastline is revealing new information about people who were enslaved centuries ago, but also destroying sites of historical and cultural importance.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9dd4ad48-97ee-11f1-b596-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AAAB-sep59-60-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9dd4ad48-97ee-11f1-b596-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AAAB-sep59-60-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5a0474c0-9a39-11f1-8ac6-db7960a1f159</guid><pubDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 15:07:27 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9dd4ad48-97ee-11f1-b596-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AAAB-sep59-60-1.jpg">© Thomas Romon / Inrap</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Ravaged by wildfires, France's Fontainebleau forest reopens to public</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260822-france-s-fontainebleau-forest-reopens-to-public-after-wildfires</link><description>
The forest of Fontainebleau outside Paris has partially reopened to the public after remaining off-limits for over a month due to devastating wildfires. From Saturday, visitors can access some 80 percent of the forest, but are being warned to show caution around fragile wildlife and charred trees.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2739da80-91b0-11f1-80fe-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Une-vue-a%C3%A9rienne-montre-une-zone-br%C3%BBl%C3%A9e-%C3%A0-la-suite-d-un-incendie-de-for%C3%AAt-dans-la-for%C3%AAt-de-Fontainebleau-%C3%A0-Noisy-sur-%C3%89cole-en-%C3%8Ele-de-France-le-30-juillet-2026.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2739da80-91b0-11f1-80fe-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Une-vue-a%C3%A9rienne-montre-une-zone-br%C3%BBl%C3%A9e-%C3%A0-la-suite-d-un-incendie-de-for%C3%AAt-dans-la-for%C3%AAt-de-Fontainebleau-%C3%A0-Noisy-sur-%C3%89cole-en-%C3%8Ele-de-France-le-30-juillet-2026.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">33b21100-9e04-11f1-bb3d-976fc488f692</guid><pubDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 09:45:36 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2739da80-91b0-11f1-80fe-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Une-vue-a%C3%A9rienne-montre-une-zone-br%C3%BBl%C3%A9e-%C3%A0-la-suite-d-un-incendie-de-for%C3%AAt-dans-la-for%C3%AAt-de-Fontainebleau-%C3%A0-Noisy-sur-%C3%89cole-en-%C3%8Ele-de-France-le-30-juillet-2026.jpg">© AFP - SIMON WOHLFAHRT </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French farmers dip into winter fodder as drought leaves pastures bare</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260822-french-farmers-dip-into-winter-fodder-as-drought-leaves-pastures-bare</link><description>
Repeated heatwaves and drought have made it a punishing summer for French farmers – scorching pastures, straining livestock and driving up costs. With grass disappearing from fields, cattle farmers across the country are already dipping into fodder meant to feed their herds through winter.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a3244506-9d43-11f1-9c0d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Cattle-farmer-Philippe-Dufour-s-cows-are-now-being-fed-in-the-barn-because-the-pastures-have-dried-out-August-2026-Credit-Zeenat-Hansrod.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a3244506-9d43-11f1-9c0d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Cattle-farmer-Philippe-Dufour-s-cows-are-now-being-fed-in-the-barn-because-the-pastures-have-dried-out-August-2026-Credit-Zeenat-Hansrod.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">44161466-9d40-11f1-9260-c93d65df09a9</guid><pubDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 07:04:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a3244506-9d43-11f1-9c0d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Cattle-farmer-Philippe-Dufour-s-cows-are-now-being-fed-in-the-barn-because-the-pastures-have-dried-out-August-2026-Credit-Zeenat-Hansrod.jpg">© Zeenat Hansrod</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France backs down on plan to make patients pay more for healthcare</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260821-france-backs-down-on-plan-to-make-patients-pay-more-for-healthcare-medicine</link><description>
The French government has scrapped plans to double the annual ceiling on out-of-pocket charges for medicines, medical appointments and other healthcare, after criticism from patient groups and health professionals. The cap was due to rise from €100 to €200, but the government will instead pursue a smaller increase linked to inflation.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/83b9c060-9d57-11f1-af31-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP20063478463590.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/83b9c060-9d57-11f1-af31-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP20063478463590.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">264a2d16-9d52-11f1-8885-2deea6adc246</guid><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 13:45:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/83b9c060-9d57-11f1-af31-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP20063478463590.jpg">AP - Daniel Cole</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Millions in France report eco-anxiety after summer of heatwaves and wildfires</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260821-millions-in-france-report-eco-anxiety-after-summer-of-heat-and-wildfires</link><description>
Record-breaking heatwaves, drought and wildfires are driving a surge in eco-anxiety across France, with some sufferers "paralysed" by panic attacks, unable to work and, in the most severe cases, experiencing suicidal thoughts.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e4a8e792-655f-11eb-b34e-005056a98db9/w:1024/p:16x9/AP19074503618238.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e4a8e792-655f-11eb-b34e-005056a98db9/w:1024/p:16x9/AP19074503618238.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4cfa3812-9c8e-11f1-9c7e-2f8d63b40800</guid><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 05:59:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e4a8e792-655f-11eb-b34e-005056a98db9/w:1024/p:16x9/AP19074503618238.jpg">AP - Claude Paris</source><dc:creator>Alison Hird with RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French hospital helicopter landings disrupted by illegal prison delivery drones</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260820-french-hospital-helicopter-landings-disrupted-by-illegal-prison-delivery-drones</link><description>
Emergency helicopter landings at Strasbourg University Hospitals have been suspended over the risk of collision with drones used to illegally deliver items to inmates in a nearby prison. The hospital says the resulting detour could be "life-threatening" for patients.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7ac3d0f0-9bee-11f1-a861-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/834848d25f61bd9c669fe2dda2e449673e221ddc.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7ac3d0f0-9bee-11f1-a861-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/834848d25f61bd9c669fe2dda2e449673e221ddc.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cbfa0aba-9c99-11f1-89cd-cf462987716b</guid><pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 15:09:01 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7ac3d0f0-9bee-11f1-a861-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/834848d25f61bd9c669fe2dda2e449673e221ddc.jpg">© Gabriel BOUYS / AFP/Archives</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>July heatwave sees 1,243 deaths in France, bringing summer toll to 7,300</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260820-july-heatwave-caused-over-1-200-deaths-in-france-bringing-summer-toll-to-7-300</link><description>
More than 1,200 excess deaths were recorded in France during the country's July heatwave, bringing the provisional death toll from extreme temperatures this year to 7,300.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0927568e-9c5b-11f1-a303-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-21T060726Z-1185403991-RC28EMAEUM4D-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-DEATHS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0927568e-9c5b-11f1-a303-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-21T060726Z-1185403991-RC28EMAEUM4D-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-DEATHS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">369b69e8-9c5b-11f1-9fd0-11ad03b15a71</guid><pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 05:51:38 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0927568e-9c5b-11f1-a303-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-21T060726Z-1185403991-RC28EMAEUM4D-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-DEATHS.jpg">© Tom Nicholson/Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French winegrowers begin record early harvest as heat and drought bite</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260820-record-early-grape-harvest-in-france-highlights-growing-impact-of-climate-change</link><description>
Drought and heatwaves have pushed French winegrowers to start picking grapes weeks ahead of schedule, with this year seeing some of the earliest harvests on record – a sign of how climate change is reshaping the wine calendar across the country.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/88c065e6-9974-11f1-8f0a-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-14T100332Z-1528940009-RC26YMAIAPDU-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-CHAMPAGNE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/88c065e6-9974-11f1-8f0a-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-14T100332Z-1528940009-RC26YMAIAPDU-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-CHAMPAGNE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">31807718-9a4f-11f1-af8a-39f218d346d1</guid><pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 04:41:16 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/88c065e6-9974-11f1-8f0a-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-14T100332Z-1528940009-RC26YMAIAPDU-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-CHAMPAGNE.jpg">© Sarah Meyssonnier/Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France's pioneering women's rights minister Yvette Roudy dies aged 97</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260819-france-s-pioneering-women-s-rights-minister-yvette-roudy-dies-aged-97</link><description>
Yvette Roudy, France's first women's rights minister and a leading figure in the country's feminist movement, has died at the age of 97.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a5cd2e92-213f-11f1-b8a4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP8111170190.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a5cd2e92-213f-11f1-b8a4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP8111170190.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">47c6feb0-9bb8-11f1-bd50-31cc77cfd92b</guid><pubDate>Wed, 19 Aug 2026 13:02:42 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a5cd2e92-213f-11f1-b8a4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP8111170190.jpg">ASSOCIATED PRESS - Herve Merliac</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France to expel two Iranian diplomats amid growing 'interference' row</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260819-france-to-expel-two-iranian-diplomats-amid-growing-interference-row</link><description>
France will expel two Iranian diplomats in the coming days in response to Iran's decision to bar two French embassy staff from returning to Tehran, Foreign Minister Jean-Noël Barrot has said.
